<p>New York authorities say two improvised explosive devices were thrown during clashes outside Gracie Mansion, the official residence of Mayor Zohran Mamdani, as an anti-Islam protest and a larger counter-protest faced off over the weekend. Police say no one was hurt, and the homemade devices did not detonate / failed to ignite. The NYPD says it is investigating the incident as “ISIS-inspired” or “IS-inspired” terrorism, working with federal prosecutors and the FBI’s Joint Terrorism Task Force. Two suspects—reported as US citizens and described in some coverage as teenagers/young men—were arrested and are expected to face terrorism-related charges. Some outlets, citing court documents, say the men expressed alignment with the Islamic State group after their arrest. City officials also called for calm, condemning anti-Muslim animus while stressing that violence has no place at demonstrations. Police leadership said preliminary bomb-squad analysis suggests the device was a real IED, not a hoax or smoke bomb, and that further testing is continuing; Dawn reported Mamdani was not home at the time.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/d7nzbe3H5vlefJ3_w_BqUziUHOS4r5oujKVe8EfQQxrKif6ODEbM7371AdNGZhCh7bjclh-4fnqRvi_JwC-DJ_Dx1csIQEnd9538d5A5S0QBmIeye-v6cfwOok3-ijk_1lKvt2oh1wyDHqGakNwvp0sAVE8K6hIAapXlnnwJg-134DGPzw' alt='New York City Police Commissioner Jessica Tisch speaks alongside Mayor Zohran Mamdani on March 9, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Device contents: Police said the thrown devices were jars wrapped in tape and packed with metal pieces such as nuts, bolts and screws—consistent with a shrapnel-producing improvised explosive.</li><li>Additional searches: Investigators searched locations linked to the suspects, including two homes in Pennsylvania, as they worked to determine whether anyone else helped plan or support the act.</li><li>Car inspection: The NYPD bomb squad inspected a vehicle linked to the suspects near the scene. Police said a suspicious item found in the car tested negative for explosives.</li><li>Alleged intent: The BBC reported the police commissioner said one suspect wanted an attack “even larger” than the Boston Marathon bombing, a detail prosecutors may cite to argue intent.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>NYPD Commissioner Jessica Tisch: She said authorities are investigating the incident as “ISIS-inspired terrorism” and that the device was real and could have caused serious injury or death. She also said investigators do not believe it was tied to the ongoing conflict in Iran. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1980194/pair-charged-with-terrorist-offences-for-throwing-explosives-near-a-protest-outside-new-york-mayor-mamdanis-residence'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Mayor Zohran Mamdani: He condemned “bigotry and racism” surrounding the anti-Mamdani/anti-Islam protest and urged New Yorkers not to answer hateful rhetoric with violence. (<a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-09-0700/violence-america-counter-protester-lights-explosive-amid-anti-mamdani-protest-utters-allahu-akbar-nyc-mayor-rips-bigotry-and-racism'>AllSides</a>)</li><li>Far-right influencer Jake Lang: He organized the demonstration outside Gracie Mansion, which news coverage described as an anti-Islam protest. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1980194/pair-charged-with-terrorist-offences-for-throwing-explosives-near-a-protest-outside-new-york-mayor-mamdanis-residence'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>FBI and federal prosecutors: They joined the investigation through the FBI’s Joint Terrorism Task Force, as local and federal authorities assess whether the act drew inspiration from ISIS tactics. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/new-york-police-investigate-explosives-thrown-near-mamdanis-residence-as-isis-related-terrorism/article70723409.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/new-york-police-investigate-explosives-thrown-near-mamdanis-residence-as-isis-related-terrorism/article70723409.ece'>New York Police investigate explosives thrown near Mamdani’s residence as ‘ISIS-related terrorism’</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/09/new-york-police-say-bomb-incident-near-mayor-s-residence-investigated-as-is-inspired-terrorism_6751250_4.html'>New York police say bomb incident near mayor&#x27;s residence investigated as IS-inspired &#x27;terrorism&#x27;</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/usa/2026-03-09/new-york-police-investigating-possible-jihadist-motivation-behind-attack-near-zohran-mamdanis-residence.html'>New York police investigating possible jihadist motivation behind attack on far-right march near Zohran Mamdani’s residence</a> - elpais.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/us-investigators-looking-at-isis-motive-in-ny-bomb-attack/a-76283429'>US: Investigators looking at ISIS motive in NY bomb attack</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/09/two-teenagers-detained-for-using-is-inspired-devices-at-a-new-york-protest'>Two teenagers detained for using &#x27;IS-inspired&#x27; devices at a New York protest</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-09-0700/violence-america-counter-protester-lights-explosive-amid-anti-mamdani-protest-utters-allahu-akbar-nyc-mayor-rips-bigotry-and-racism'>Counter-protester lights explosive amid anti-Mamdani protest, utters &#x27;Allahu Akbar&#x27; — but NYC mayor rips &#x27;bigotry and racism&#x27;</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/two-men-charged-with-terrorism-after-homemade-bomb-thrown-at-anti-islam-protesters-in-new-york'>2 men charged with terrorism after bomb thrown at anti-Islam protesters outside NY mayor’s home</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1980194/pair-charged-with-terrorist-offences-for-throwing-explosives-near-a-protest-outside-new-york-mayor-mamdanis-